solution.p:
We start with the equation s(1-m)=w and substitute in what we know. The value for m should be 0.9 and the value for w should be 17.5\text{.} So we have the equation
\begin{aligned}
s(1-0.9) \amp= 17.5\\
s(0.1) \amp= 17.5
\end{aligned}
Now to solve for s\text{,} divide on each side by 0.1\text{:}
\begin{aligned}
\divideunder{s(0.1)}{0.1} \amp= \divideunder{17.5}{0.1}\\
s \amp= {175}
\end{aligned}
So the shelf price is $175.
